- Use CMake (3.20+) as the build system; prefer Ninja as the generator.
- Support multi-platform builds (Windows, Linux, macOS).
- Use CMake FetchContent or Git submodules for dependencies.
- Organize build targets modularly to allow selective inclusion of features.
- Provide separate build configs: Debug, Release, RelWithDebInfo.
- Integrate unit tests with CTest.
- Enable Clang-Tidy and Clang-Format for all code.
- Check for null dereferences and memory leaks in CI/builds.
- Enforce code style and analysis rules from the coding style rule.
- No proprietary or costly tools; only open, proven libraries.

